  "worked_solution": "First, we need to determine whether $D$ is diagonalizable over $R.$\n\nWe start by computing the eigenvalues of $A.$ To do that, we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 0 & -6 \\\\ 14 & 3-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -6 \\\\ 3 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda )+18) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the quadratic polynomial  $\\,{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +8\\,$ we have that the discriminant $D<0.$ So, it doesn't have real roots. \n\nTherefore, $A$ is not diagonalizable over $R.$",
